 artifact/cache/executable, modify runtime/plugins, or change legacy
 `ir.compile`.
+
+## NVIDIA Artifact v1
+
+`Artifact` is the immutable, pointer-free output envelope for the first strict
+structured TensorIR path. It stores one Cubin together with the exact target,
+producer, kernel ABI, loader ABI, request identity, build-specification
+identity, and SHA-256 projections needed by a later cache and loader. It does
+not contain a CUDA module, function, context, stream, allocation, workspace
+pointer, tensor pointer, framework object, or runtime callback.
+
+Strict construction is:
+
+```python
+artifact = Artifact.create_strict(request, build_spec, producer_result)
+restored = Artifact.deserialize(artifact.serialize(), request, build_spec)
+assert restored.identity_digest == artifact.identity_digest
+```
+
+The compiled backend identity is not an argument. `create_strict()` obtains the
+private build anchor internally, and C++ cannot construct an arbitrary
+`NvidiaBackendBuildInfo`. The producer toolchain must match the compiled PyPTO,
+TensorIR, CUDA Tile, LLVM, CUDA toolkit, and `tileiras` identities exactly.
+Backend-OFF builds still compile the data model, but strict construction fails
+closed.
+
+### Exact producer and target contract
+
+Artifact v1 accepts only:
+
+- `SemanticRoute.StructuredTensorIr`;
+- Cubin requested and produced, with no fallback;
+- exact numeric SM 120 and TensorIR exact target `sm_120a`;
+- CUDA Tile bytecode version 13.3.0;
+- `layout-propagation`, one CTA, four worker warps, no online candidate search,
+  no environment overrides, and `uniform_signature=false`;
+- tile sizes named contiguously as `dim_000`, `dim_001`, and so on.
+
+The assembler CLI spelling and semantic target are separate identity fields:
+`assembler_gpu_name=sm_120`, while TensorIR's exact-architecture policy is
+`tensor_ir_target=sm_120a`. The canonical pipeline specification is
+[`structured_tensorir_explicit_v1.json`](../../../../src/compiler/nvidia/structured_tensorir_explicit_v1.json).
+Its Git-blob identity is `a5398054a515c632506c3f1ffa3a0b5d9e819e83`;
+CMake verifies that identity so the pipeline revision cannot be an unexplained
+placeholder.
+
+Resolved schedule metadata is cross-checked against the reconstructed kernel
+ABI. In particular, grid tile sizes must equal the schedule tile sizes, and
+the argument layout must agree with `uniform_signature=false`. The complete
+kernel ABI is also bound by `KernelBuildSpec.callable_abi_digest`.
+
+### Runtime-free Cubin and parameter-ABI validation
+
+The private TensorIR validator performs no CUDA call, device query, filesystem
+access, module load, or subprocess execution. For the pinned CUDA 13.3 Cubin
+format it checks:
+
+- complete ELF64 tables, sections, segments, CUDA OSABI/ABI, and numeric SM;
+- one declared global/weak CUDA entry function (`STT_FUNC` plus
+  `STO_CUDA_ENTRY`) whose non-empty range is inside executable
+  `.text.<entry>` bytes;
+- linked `.nv.info.<entry>` and `.nv.constant0.<entry>` sections;
+- every flattened `KPARAM_INFO` ordinal, byte width, non-overlapping parameter
+  range, and `CBANK_PARAM_SIZE` extent.
+
+Tensor operands contribute an 8-byte pointer. Dynamic sizes and strides are
+4-byte kernel parameters in the pinned TensorIR CUDA Tile ABI. Scalar operands
+use their explicit descriptor width. This catches a valid Cubin paired with a
+different static, dynamic, or scalar launch signature; entry-name checking
+alone would not.
+
+This validator attests structure, target, entry, and launch parameter ABI. It
+does not independently disassemble or prove SASS instruction semantics. Those
+bytes must come from the exact private `tileiras` producer recorded in the
+artifact.
+
+### Canonical storage and identities
+
+The full Artifact is canonical MessagePack with one binary field. The payload
+is capped at 68 MiB and device code at 64 MiB. A streaming preflight bounds
+maps, arrays, strings, binary fields, total objects, aggregate container items,
+non-binary bytes, and nesting before object-tree allocation. During
+deserialization the Cubin BIN may borrow the input only within the call; it is
+copied into the returned immutable value before the input can expire, and
+rvalue backing storage is rejected at compile time.
+
+Separate SHA-256 projections are provided for complete artifact identity,
+precompile cache identity, producer options, callable kernel ABI, and loader
+compatibility. Deserialization revalidates the expected request/build
+identities, Cubin SHA-256, strict producer contract, target, entry/parameter
+ABI, and byte-for-byte canonical encoding.
